<section class="section band" id="harnesses">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Forty harnesses, read where they already write.</h2>
    <ul class="harness-list">
      <li><HarnessIcon slug="claude" />Claude Code</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="opencode" />OpenCode</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="codex" />Codex CLI</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="gemini" />Gemini CLI</li>
      <li><HarnessIcon slug="copilot" />Copilot CLI</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="amp" />Amp</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="qwen" />Qwen Code</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="goose" />Goose</li>
      <li><HarnessIcon slug="cline" />Cline</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="roocode" />Roo Code</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="zed" />Zed Agent</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="grok" />Grok CLI</li>
      <li><HarnessIcon slug="kilocode" />Kilo Code CLI</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="junie" />Junie</li><li><HarnessIcon slug="devin" />Devin CLI</li><li class="more">and 25 more</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">Nothing to install into the harness. No plugin, no proxy, no exporter. Skopli parses the session state each one keeps on disk.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap" id="honest">
  <div class="refuse-grid">
    <div class="refuse-copy">
      <h2>What Skopli refuses to do.</h2>
      <p class="note">Four of them. A wrong number is worse than a gap you can see.</p>
      <dl class="refuse">
        <div><dt>Guess a price</dt><dd>An unmatched model returns <code>priced: false</code> with the catalogs it checked, and stays out of the total.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Send telemetry</dt><dd>No telemetry or analytics calls, ever. It measures your agents, not you. Pricing fetches market catalogs only when you opt into the Price layer, and caches what it fetches.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Require an account</dt><dd>Nothing to sign up for. It runs offline against files you already have.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Double-count tokens</dt><dd>Input, output, and cache tokens stay in separate buckets. Claude's 5-minute and 1-hour cache writes are split and priced apart.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <figure class="miss-card">
      <div class="code">
        <div class="code-head"><span class="file">an unmatched model, reported in full</span><span class="reg">Skopli</span></div>
        <pre><code>{'{'}
  model<span class="pn">:</span> <span class="str">"local-fine-tune"</span><span class="pn">,</span>
  tokens<span class="pn">:</span> {'{'} input<span class="pn">:</span> <span class="no">6332410</span><span class="pn">,</span> output<span class="pn">:</span> <span class="no">401092</span> {'}'}<span class="pn">,</span>
  priced<span class="pn">:</span> <span class="bad">false</span><span class="pn">,</span>
  attempted<span class="pn">:</span> <span class="pn">[</span><span class="str">"openrouter"</span><span class="pn">,</span> <span class="str">"litellm"</span><span class="pn">,</span> <span class="str">"models.dev"</span><span class="pn">]</span>
  <span class="cm">// no rate found, so none invented</span>
{'}'}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="prior-art">
  <div class="wrap prior">
    <h2>Why a library.</h2>
    <p>Skopli ships read, rollup, and price as a library, so what you build on top is yours: a dashboard, a nightly report, a CI budget check, a billing reconciliation. Reach for Skopli when you need these numbers inside your own code.</p>
  </div>
</section>

